WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.503
-Several pools --
Several polls -- excuse me --

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.673
including one by Fox News
itself, have now shown

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.908
that President Biden's
vaccine requirements

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.144
and other COVID measures
are widely popular,

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.079
so Republicans
and right-wing pundits

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.514
have been forced to come up

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.349
with increasingly insane
arguments against them.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.183
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:21.687 line:0%
[ Theme music plays ]

00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.022
One way you can tell

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.391
that the Republican Party
is intellectually bankrupt is

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.460
that they spend very little time
talking about policy,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.928
and a lot more time
talking about

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.731
bat[Bleep] conspiracy theories
they concocted out of nowhere.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.400
It's so hard to keep up with
the right-wing rumor mill

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.602
that sometimes
I'll only find out about one

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:38.605
after it's been debunked.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.039
Yesterday, I was scrolling
through Twitter

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.575
and saw a Snopes headline
that said, "No, Joe Biden

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.110
is Not a Westworld Robot
Created by George Soros

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.613
to Steal your Hamburgers."
And I thought, "Oh, right,

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:50.950 line:0%
I forgot to tape
Judge Jeanine last night."

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.685
Say what you want
about the Democrats --

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.188
and there's plenty to criticize
about centrists

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.023
standing in the way
of major legislation --

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.625
but at least the progressives
in the party,

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.326
like Budget Committee
Chairman Bernie Sanders,

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:03.629
are trying to pass
a $3.5 trillion package

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:04.764
that would, among other things,

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.732
establish a universal
pre-K program

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:09.068
and a new childcare benefit
for working families,

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.370
extend the expansions
of the child tax credit,

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.005
the earned income tax credit,

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:14.973
and child and dependent care
tax credit,

00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:18.044
create the first federal
paid and medical leave benefit,

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.880
add dental, vision, and hearing
benefits to Medicare,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.549
and make investments
aiming to meet Biden's goals

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:26.719
of reducing economy-wide
carbon emissions by 50%.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.821
And in defense of the bill,

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.324
Bernie has deployed some of his
trademark sarcasm.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.193
-I understand
that Senator McConnell,

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.595
the Republican leader,
and others

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:40.333
are really shocked by this bill.
They cannot believe it.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.502
Imagine!
Just imagine

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:46.739
that the United States Senate

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:50.209
is addressing
the needs of working families

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.612
and is gonna stand up
for ordinary Americans,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.250
rather than just
the wealthy and powerful.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.486
What is this world coming to?

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.289
Don't we understand
that here in the Senate,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.959
we're supposed
to take campaign contributions

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.962
from the drug companies
and the insurance companies

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:13.032
and the fossil-fuel industry,

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:16.102
and from the 1%,
and do their bidding?

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.938
Isn't that the way
it has always been done

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.007
here in the U.S. Senate?

00:02:22.007 --> 00:02:25.411
Well, Senator McConnell,
things are changing.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.179
-I like that Bernie
takes on the right

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:28.848
the same way he takes on
a waiter

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.850
who brings him soup
but no spoon.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.418
[As Sanders]
"Oh, this is fantastic.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:35.989
Soup without a spoon.
Maybe I'll just use my fork,

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.558
famously designed
for use with liquids.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:42.428
Or maybe you'd be good enough
to bring me

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.830
one of those
wide McDonald's straws

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.499
so I don't give myself
an aneurysm

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.801
trying to get
the chicken chunks up."

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.902
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.238
[ Normal voice ] So...

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:55.975
the left is focused on trying
to pass a far-reaching bill

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.811
that would transform childcare,
expand the social safety net,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.713
and tackle climate change,
among other things.

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:03.082
And what's the MAGA crowd doing?

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.152
Are they offering
any alternative solutions?

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.920
Or are they asking Eric Trump

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.956
about Nicki Minaj's cousin's
friend's swollen balls?

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:13.125
-We saw what happened
to Nicki Minaj this week.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.627
She's facing backlash

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.329
for tweeting
to her 22 million followers

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:22.101
that a friend of her cousin
had issues with the vaccine,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.772
and now they're
trying to cancel her.

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:28.607
-Well, that's exactly right.

00:03:28.607 --> 00:03:29.608
They'll try
and cancel everybody.

00:03:29.608 --> 00:03:31.076
I've lived cancel culture

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:33.012
probably better
than any person in the world.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.447
And if you speak out
against them,

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.150
if you disagree with them,
they cancel you,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.720
they try and arrest you,
they try and prosecute you.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.223
It's amazing kind of the, you
know, unjustice in this country.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.426
And America was always
this country that stood for,

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:49.461
you know, equal weights of
justice on both sides.

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:51.230
I mean, it's a national
symbol of ours,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.099
the scales of justice.
We don't have that anymore.

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:56.201
It reminds me of
a banana republic, Maria.

00:03:56.201 --> 00:03:57.470
It really does.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.139
-First of all, you doofus,
the scales of justice

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:02.742
are not "equal weights
on both sides."

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.311
The whole point is that
the evidence on one side

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.413
outweighs the evidence
on the other.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.882
That's why court cases
never end in ties.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.583
Also, who said
Nicki Minaj is canceled?

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:13.219
I mean, I disagree with her
on vaccines,

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.621
and I think spreading
misinformation is dangerous,

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.156
but she's still
an amazing artist.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:20.059
And if her next song rhymed
"vax," "sacks,"

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.729
and "Biden, call me back,"
I'd be happier than anyone.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:24.430
It's also great
when the same people

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.166
who scream "fake news"
treat a Nicki Minaj tweet

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:29.101
about her
cousin's friend's balls

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.703
like it's
unimpeachable information.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.772
She just tweeted
a rumor she heard

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.006
that obviously wasn't true.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.676
She's not reporting live
outside a hospital on CNN.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:40.246
"Day eight of ball watch.
We go now live to Nicki Minaj."

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:43.949
Also, if something reminds
Eric Trump of a banana republic,

00:04:43.949 --> 00:04:46.084
it's probably referring
to a time

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:48.020
he thinks he was treated rudely
at the store.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.222
"Maria, this whole thing
reminds me of being told

00:04:50.222 --> 00:04:52.357
I could only bring seven items
into the dressing room

00:04:52.357 --> 00:04:53.792
at one time,
to which I said,

00:04:53.792 --> 00:04:56.562
'Maybe you should have a smaller
collection of chinos.'"

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.798
But that isn't even the weirdest
topic of conversation

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:02.201
Maria Bartiromo entertained
on her show this weekend.

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.037
In the same hour,
she also asked Ted Cruz

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:07.506
about a conspiracy theory
that the White House

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.042
has been cutting off
Joe Biden's microphone,

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.811
which has already been debunked
by fact checkers,

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:15.080
as well as reality.
And Cruz went along with it.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.050
-President Biden's microphone
apparently looked like

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.919
it was cut off at one point
this past week.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:24.791
Do you believe he's making
these decisions on Afghanistan

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:28.093
and -- and
these leadership missteps?

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:31.364
-Well, I would say
it's a disturbing pattern

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.199
where it seems they cut off
his microphone

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:36.502
anytime he might say something
that his handlers don't want.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.938
There's no doubt
that President Biden's capacity

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:42.307
is severely diminished,
and his White House handlers

00:05:42.307 --> 00:05:45.845
amplify that impression
when they keep him locked up

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.746
in a basement all day long.

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:49.448
-You know, they tried
this basement line

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:51.284
in the campaign,
and it didn't work,

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.286
probably because it wasn't true,
and even if it was,

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.354
after four years of Trump,
voters were thinking,

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:58.257
"A basement president
doesn't sound that bad."

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.159
They're also
probably super bummed

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.228
that if a mute button exists,
they didn't use it for Trump.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:05.464
"Could have used it during
that Boy Scouts speech."

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.400
But apparently this mic
canceling button theory,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.837
repeatedly debunked, is a thing
in right-wing circles --

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:13.339
so much so that it's been
repeated on Fox News

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:17.143
and even in an official hearing
of the United States Senate.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:19.278
-I don't know.
Is somebody telling him

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:21.481
that he can't continue,
and now are they to the point

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:25.251
where they're controlling when
he has to end his speaking?

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.486
-Has he thought or read anything

00:06:27.486 --> 00:06:29.021
that people are writing
about him

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:31.123
and how they cut off
his microphone

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.391
rather than ask questions?

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.594
-Somebody in the White House
has authority

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:37.129
to press the button
and stop the president --

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:40.399
cut off the president's
speaking ability and sound.

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:42.535
Who is that person?
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.270
-I think anyone
who knows the president,

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.105
including members
of this committee,

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:49.074
knows that he speaks
very clearly

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:51.911
and very deliberately
for himself.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.779
No one else does.

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:55.548
-Well, are you saying

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:57.716
that there is no one
in the White House

00:06:57.716 --> 00:07:00.052
that can cut him off?
Because yesterday that happened,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.920
and it's happened
a number of times before that.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:05.491
It's been widely reported
that somebody has the ability

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.994
to push the button
and cut off his sound

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:10.663
and stop him from speaking.
Who is that person?

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.499
-There is --
There is no such person.

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:16.368
-Are you telling this committee
that this does not happen,

00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:18.671
that there's no one
in the White House

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:19.938
who pushes the button and
cuts him off in midsentence?

00:07:19.938 --> 00:07:22.942
-[ Chuckles ]
That's correct.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.244
-First of all,
if a button like that existed,

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:27.914
Shoemaker would have it for me,
because he is a power-hungry --

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:30.950
[ No audio ]

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.018
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.118
Second, how psyched do you think

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:35.120
Secretary of State
Antony Blinken was,

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.790
not even a month after
the Afghanistan withdrawal,

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:41.794
to get to field questions about
a nonexistent mute button?

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.395
What's next?
"Now, Secretary Blinken,

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:46.165
I want to ask you
about the Americans

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:47.966
still trying
to leave Afghanistan.

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:50.569
But before I do,
does the president

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:53.739
tape pictures of naked ladies on
the inside of his aviators?"

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.841
Also, anytime you find yourself

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:57.243
on the same page
as Brian Kilmeade,

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.744
that's a hint
you're doing it wrong.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:00.879
It's like looking over
during the S.A.T.s

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:02.981
and realizing you have
the same answers

00:08:02.981 --> 00:08:05.184
as the kid who has to sing
"The Bunny Rabbit Song"

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:06.518
to tie his shoes.

00:08:06.518 --> 00:08:08.754
"Psst, do you have the answers
written on your hand?"

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:11.123
"Oh, no, that's just 'S.A.T.,'

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.959
so I don't forget
what test I'm taking."

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:15.160
This is what the right
is talking about,

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.862
rather than actual policy.
And that's because

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:19.331
Biden's COVID policies
are fairly popular

00:08:19.331 --> 00:08:20.733
with a majority of Americans.

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:22.768 line:0%
including his newly announced
vaccine mandate,

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:26.238 line:0%
which multiple polls have now
shown have majority support.

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:29.375 line:0%
In fact, even a Fox News poll,
out this weekend,

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.243 line:0%
found that voters support
mask mandates

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:33.679 line:0%
and Biden's
new vaccine requirements,

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:35.848 line:0%
whether in businesses,
indoor establishments,

00:08:35.848 --> 00:08:37.016 line:0%
or schools.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:40.052
-69% of people say
that wearing a mask

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:43.055
is a good way to help,
and 54% of people

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:45.290
support mandatory
proof of vaccine

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.693
to enter indoor establishments.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:50.195
-The survey found
a majority of respondents

00:08:50.195 --> 00:08:52.331
support mask and vaccine
mandates

00:08:52.331 --> 00:08:54.233
for schools and businesses.

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:57.503
-It's always funny to me when
Fox conducts an accurate poll

00:08:57.503 --> 00:08:59.071
that contradicts what
their own hosts

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.272
are telling their audience.

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:02.240
That's as damning
as the results of their poll,

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.109
"Do you think Joe Biden
lives in the basement,

00:09:04.109 --> 00:09:05.945
or a different part
of the White House?"

00:09:05.945 --> 00:09:07.880
I mean, their own polling
is telling them

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.648
mask and vaccine mandates
are popular

00:09:09.648 --> 00:09:11.016
with a majority of Americans,

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:13.619
and yet their hosts are still
saying stuff like this.

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:16.522
-If they can force you to take
a vaccine that you don't need,

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:19.391
what can't they do?

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:23.462
Why don't they, I don't know,
make you take psychiatric drugs

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.330
if you're
persistently disobedient;

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.232
express the wrong view,
get a Thorazine shot?

00:09:27.232 --> 00:09:28.333
Why couldn't they do that?

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.335
What's the limiting principle
on them?

00:09:30.335 --> 00:09:33.405
In fact, you can imagine a panel
of CNN doctors who explained

00:09:33.405 --> 00:09:36.408
that we'd all be a lot safer if
the mentally-ill propagandists

00:09:36.408 --> 00:09:39.077
on the radical right
got the treatment they need

00:09:39.077 --> 00:09:41.814
and stop spreading their
dangerous conspiracy theories.

00:09:41.814 --> 00:09:43.615
So giving them psychotropic meds

00:09:43.615 --> 00:09:46.351
is an urgent matter
of public health.

00:09:46.351 --> 00:09:48.888
Does that sound far-fetched?
[ Chuckles ]

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:51.557
-Why is Tucker so concerned

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:53.459
that someone might give him
psychotropic drugs?

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:56.128
It's awfully specific for him
to use as a random example.

00:09:56.128 --> 00:09:58.730
Did it come up recently,
like, at his last physical?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.033
"Alright, Tucker, mostly great.
Blood pressure a little high.

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:02.601
And have you ever thought
about Thorazine?"

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:05.037
Also, if you don't want people
recommending psychotropic meds,

00:10:05.037 --> 00:10:07.907
try to drop that quiet chuckle
you did to yourself.

00:10:07.907 --> 00:10:10.342
You never see a guy sitting
on a bench in Central Park

00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:11.443
laughing at nothing,
and think,

00:10:11.443 --> 00:10:13.745
"I'm gonna go ask that guy
for stock tips."

00:10:13.745 --> 00:10:15.081
I will say this, though.

00:10:15.081 --> 00:10:16.749
If cable news ever gets boring
for Tucker,

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:18.050
he'd make
a hell of an improviser,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.251
because my man knows
how to heighten.

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.587
"If they can force you
to take a vaccine,

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:23.922
what can't they force you to do?

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:25.924
Can they force you
to take psychotropic meds?

00:10:25.924 --> 00:10:27.159
Make you wear a seat belt?

00:10:27.159 --> 00:10:29.528
Make you put your shoes on
at Olive Garden,

00:10:29.528 --> 00:10:32.531
even though they tell you, 'When
you're here, you're family'?"

00:10:32.531 --> 00:10:34.933
[ Laughter ]

00:10:34.933 --> 00:10:36.468
"And then, when you try
to fill a briefcase

00:10:36.468 --> 00:10:38.971
with unlimited breadsticks,
can they call security?

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.373
And when you explain to them
that if they didn't want people

00:10:41.373 --> 00:10:42.875
to put breadsticks
in their suitcases,

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:45.010
they should put a sign up
saying as much,

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.979
can they then roll their eyes
and say, 'Let's please

00:10:46.979 --> 00:10:48.680
not do this again, Mr. Carlson,
because it's

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.215
the same argument you made
the last time you were there.'

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:52.284
And when you say, 'You could
put the sign right there,'

00:10:52.284 --> 00:10:53.652
and point to the wall
behind them,

00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:55.354
and then run for the front door
when they turn around,

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.856
only to crash
into the hostess station,

00:10:56.856 --> 00:10:58.590
can they stand over you,
pointing and laughing?

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.126
Well, I'm here to tell you,
they can,

00:11:01.126 --> 00:11:03.829
because it happened to me
last night."

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:06.031
[ Laughter ]
"[ Fake chuckles ]"

00:11:06.031 --> 00:11:08.133
[ Laughter ]

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:10.369
Every day, it just
becomes clearer and clearer

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:12.204
that these guys have no idea
what they're talking about.

00:11:12.204 --> 00:11:14.073
For example,
Congressman Madison Cawthorn

00:11:14.073 --> 00:11:15.908
went on Newsmax last week
and said this.

00:11:15.908 --> 00:11:19.011
-This is a medical apartheid,
plain and simple.

00:11:19.011 --> 00:11:21.046
There's over 100 million
Americans

00:11:21.046 --> 00:11:22.247
who are not vaccinated.

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:23.415
I think it's
even more than that.

00:11:23.415 --> 00:11:26.719
And if they want to start
shutting down air travel

00:11:26.719 --> 00:11:28.219
for these people
to get around the country,

00:11:28.219 --> 00:11:30.522
I think that's actually
a Constitutional violation,

00:11:30.522 --> 00:11:33.192
because you actually have a
constitutionally protected right

00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:35.127
to free, unrestricted travel

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:37.062
within the
United States of America.

00:11:37.062 --> 00:11:40.332
And I genuinely believe that
what's going on right now is

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:43.235
that all that's gonna happen
if United Airlines

00:11:43.235 --> 00:11:46.038
and American Airlines and Delta,
even if they decide

00:11:46.038 --> 00:11:47.839
to start requiring
vaccine mandates,

00:11:47.839 --> 00:11:49.508
let me tell you,
I'm very confident

00:11:49.508 --> 00:11:51.610
there will be
another air carrier

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:54.946
that will come to the field, and
patriots like myself and you

00:11:54.946 --> 00:11:57.048
will give them
all of our business.

00:11:57.048 --> 00:11:59.585
-Yes, everyone knows you have
a constitutional right

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:01.319
to unrestricted air travel.
Who can forget

00:12:01.319 --> 00:12:03.456
Paul Revere's famous words,
"One if by land,

00:12:03.456 --> 00:12:05.490
two if by sea,
three if by Southwest

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.559
with a six-hour layover
at Chicago-Midway."

00:12:07.559 --> 00:12:09.094
Also, imagine
if what he said came true,

00:12:09.094 --> 00:12:10.429
and there was an airline

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:11.931
that specifically served
the unvaccinated.

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.600
"No frills, no rules, all chaos.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.768
At Patriot Airlines,
you don't board by group number,

00:12:16.768 --> 00:12:18.404
you board based on
how much you love America,

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:20.072
and there will be disagreements.

00:12:20.072 --> 00:12:22.941
Allergic to peanuts? Too bad!
We put it in the coffee.

00:12:22.941 --> 00:12:25.745
And the armrest always belongs
to whoever wants it the most.

00:12:25.745 --> 00:12:27.780
Patriot Airlines,
where the arrival gate

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.781
always has
a team of air marshals

00:12:29.781 --> 00:12:32.150
waiting to make arrests."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:33.885
These guys really think
the constitution says

00:12:33.885 --> 00:12:35.387
you have the right
to get on an airplane

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.623
unvaccinated and
cough all over everyone.

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:39.357
although, as we know,
there are apparently

00:12:39.357 --> 00:12:41.927
some prominent Republicans
who do believe airplanes

00:12:41.927 --> 00:12:44.163
were around during the writing
of the Constitution.

00:12:44.163 --> 00:12:48.334
-The Continental Army suffered
a bitter winter of Valley Forge,

00:12:48.334 --> 00:12:51.670
found glory across the waters
of the Delaware,

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:55.707
and seized victory from
Cornwallis of Yorktown.

00:12:55.707 --> 00:13:00.713
Our army manned the airports.
It rammed the ramparts.

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:04.583
It took over the airports.
It did everything it had to do.

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.886
-When that speech was over,
even Trump wished

00:13:06.886 --> 00:13:08.620
his staff had a mute button.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.956
"Did I say 'airports'
instead of 'ramparts?'"

00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:12.491
"I'm afraid so, Mr. President."

00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:14.526
"Well, next time,
hit the [Bleep] button!"

00:13:14.526 --> 00:13:15.860
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:18.029
"That's what the button's for.
That's why I do this.

00:13:18.029 --> 00:13:20.298
You know
how you press a button?"

00:13:20.298 --> 00:13:22.300
[ Laughter ]
Progressives are pushing forward

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.570
with a transformative bill
that would expand healthcare,

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.938
widen the social safety net,
and tackle climate change,

00:13:26.938 --> 00:13:28.273
among many other things.

00:13:28.273 --> 00:13:30.776
Meanwhile, the GOP has
no interest in debating ideas,

00:13:30.776 --> 00:13:32.344
so, instead, they melt down
about vaccines

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:35.013
and make up conspiracies
about presidential mute buttons.

00:13:35.013 --> 00:13:36.848
These guys
shouldn't be in Congress.

00:13:36.848 --> 00:13:38.183
They're barely qualified
to work at...

00:13:38.183 --> 00:13:40.685
-A Banana Republic.
